   "id": "yoma.70b.12",
   "daf": "70b",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "קִידֵּשׁ יָדָיו וְרַגְלָיו. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וּבָא אַהֲרֹן אֶל אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד״. לָמָה הוּא בָּא? לְהוֹצִיא אֶת הַכַּף וְאֶת הַמַּחְתָּה,",
   "en": "§ It was taught in the mishna: The High Priest «sanctified his hands and feet» and entered the Holy of Holies to take out the incense spoon and the coal pan. The Gemara cites a related baraita. «The Sages taught:» The verse states: «“And Aaron shall come into the Tent of Meeting”» (Leviticus 16:23), which is taken to mean that he enters the Holy of Holies. «Why does he come?» He comes in order «to take out the» incense «spoon and the coal pan»"
  }
 ],
